{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a cobbler-scaffold \"stitch\" task #5381 for the go-unix-utils project. The task is to implement `cmd/tr` (character translation utility) covering SRD054 requirements R1.1 through R1.4 — the fundamental character-by-character translation features. This is the initial implementation; later tasks will add delete mode (-d), squeeze mode (-s), complement mode (-c), and other features from SRD R2.x-R4.x groups.\n\n   Specific deliverables:\n   - Create `cmd/tr/main.go` with tr translation logic\n   - Create `cmd/tr/tr_test.go` with differential tests against `gtr` reference binary\n   - Implement R1.1 (basic SET1→SET2 translation with SET2 extension), R1.2 (stdin→stdout only), R1.3 (ranges, octal/backslash escapes, repetition in SET specs), R1.4 (POSIX character classes in SETs)\n   - Code must be structured for future extension (D4)\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Differential testing pattern**: Use `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` for Go binary, `exec.LookPath(\"gtr\")` for reference, `t.Skip` if not found, `testutils.RunDiffTests` to compare\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - **SET specification parsing**: Must handle individual chars, ranges (a-z), octal escapes (\\NNN), backslash escapes (\\n, \\t, \\\\, \\a, \\b, \\f, \\r, \\v), repetition ([CHAR*N], [CHAR*]), and POSIX character classes ([:alnum:], [:alpha:], [:blank:], [:cntrl:], [:digit:], [:graph:], [:lower:], [:print:], [:punct:], [:space:], [:upper:], [:xdigit:])\n   - **Translation table**: 256-byte mapping table where SET1[i] maps to SET2[i]; if SET2 is shorter, last character of SET2 repeats\n   - **LC_ALL=C**: All tests must use C locale (single-byte encoding only, per non_goals)\n   - **No file arguments**: tr reads exclusively from stdin per POSIX\n   - **Function size limit**: 40 lines hard limit per function (E8)\n   - **File size limit**: 500 lines per Go source file (E9)\n   - **Copyright header**: Every file must start with SPDX copyright header\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd054-tr.yaml** (READ)\n     - Full SRD for tr utility with requirements R1 (Character translation), R2 (Delete/squeeze), R3 (Class translation pairs), R4 (Exit codes/testing)\n     - This task only covers R1.1-R1.4\n     - Key requirements:\n       - R1.1: Translate SET1 chars to SET2 chars, extend SET2 with last char if shorter\n       - R1.2: Read stdin, write stdout, no file args\n       - R1.3: Ranges, octal escapes, backslash escapes, repetition in SET specs\n       - R1.4: POSIX character classes support\n     - Non-goals: No multibyte support, no file arguments\n   \n   - **cmd/tr/main.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - tr implementation covering R1.1-R1.4\n     - Must call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n     - Must parse SET1 and SET2 from args\n     - Must build translation table and process stdin→stdout\n   \n   - **cmd/tr/tr_test.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - Differential tests comparing Go binary against gtr\n     - Must use testutils.BuildBinary and RunDiffTests pattern\n     - Must cover: basic translation, character ranges, POSIX classes, case conversion, octal escapes, backslash escapes, SET2 extension behavior\n\n   - **Existing pkg/ source code** (PROVIDED IN CONTEXT)\n     - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` - DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests function\n     - `pkg/testutils/build.go` - BuildBinary function\n     - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` - InstallSIGPIPEHandler function\n     - All other pkg/ files provided inline\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — only one tool call (Read of the SRD) was made before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the full scope of R1.1-R1.4 requirements\n   - Identified that this task needs full SET parsing (character classes, ranges, escapes, repetition) but only the translation mode (no -d, -s, -c flags)\n   - Need to structure code for future extension per D4\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive stitch task prompt with all project context, task description, constraints, execution constitution, go style constitution, SRD references, and instructions to implement cmd/tr R1.1-R1.4\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — requesting a detailed summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/tr/main.go` implementing:\n     - SET specification parser (ranges, escapes, character classes, repetition)\n     - 256-byte translation table construction\n     - stdin→stdout translation loop\n     - SIGPIPE handler installation\n     - Proper error handling and exit codes\n   - Create `cmd/tr/tr_test.go` with differential tests covering:\n     - Basic character translation (e.g., 'abc' 'xyz')\n     - Case conversion via ranges ('a-z' 'A-Z')\n     - POSIX character classes ('[:lower:]' '[:upper:]')\n     - Octal escapes\n     - Backslash escapes (\\n, \\t, etc.)\n     - SET2 extension when shorter than SET1\n     - Repetition syntax ([a*5], [a*])\n   - Verify: `go build ./cmd/tr/`, `go vet ./cmd/tr/`, `go test ./cmd/tr/ -count=1`\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just read the SRD file `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd054-tr.yaml` to understand the full requirements for tr. I was about to plan and implement the two files (`cmd/tr/main.go` and `cmd/tr/tr_test.go`) when the summary request came in. No code has been written yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write both `cmd/tr/main.go` and `cmd/tr/tr_test.go` in full, following the go_style_constitution's implementation strategy: \"Write all source files before running any build or test commands.\" The implementation should:\n   \n   For `cmd/tr/main.go`:\n   - 