{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LG3YKznS6zMjC6o8GgiQqm","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've successfully read all the files you requested. Here's a comprehensive report on the patterns used in this Go codebase:\n\n---\n\n## Go Unix Utils - Codebase Patterns Report\n\n### 1. **cmd/cat/main.go** - Standard cmd/ Utility Structure\n\n**Copyright & Package Header:**\n- Standard copyright line: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.`\n- SPDX identifier: `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n- Descriptive package comment linking to spec: `// cmd/cat implements srd006-cat: file concatenation...`\n\n**Key Imports Pattern:**\n```go\nimport (\n    \"bufio\"\n    \"errors\"\n    \"fmt\"\n    \"io\"\n    \"os\"\n    \"syscall\"\n    \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n)\n```\n\n**SIGPIPE Handler Installation:**\n- Called immediately in `main()`: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n- Error handling checks for `syscall.EPIPE` and exits with code 0 on pipe closure\n\n**Main Structure Elements:**\n- Global flag variables (flagN, flagB, flagS, etc.)\n- `parseFlags()` function for CLI argument parsing with `--` separator support\n- File processing loop with error handling per file\n- Exit code management (0 on success, 1 on error, 0 on SIGPIPE)\n\n---\n\n### 2. **cmd/cat/cat_test.go** - Differential Testing Pattern\n\n**Test Functions:**\n- `TestDiff()`: Uses `testutils.BuildBinary()` to compile the Go binary, retrieves reference binary via `exec.LookPath(\"gcat\")`, skips if reference binary unavailable\n- `TestDiffFiles()`: Tests multi-file scenarios with temp directory fixtures\n- `TestMissingFile()`: Non-diff test for error conditions\n- `TestSIGPIPE()`: Verifies SIGPIPE handling doesn't hang the process\n\n**DiffTest Structure Usage:**\n- `Name`: Subtest identifier\n- `Args`: Command-line arguments\n- `Stdin`: Input bytes (nil = EOF, non-nil empty = open-then-close)\n- `WorkDir`: Working directory for test execution\n\n**Pattern:**\n```go\ntests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n    {Name: \"test_name\", Args: []string{\"-flag\"}, Stdin: []byte(\"data\\n\")},\n    // ... more tests\n}\ntestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n```\n\n**SIGPIPE Test Pattern:**\n- Spawns command with large output file\n- Creates stdout pipe, reads one byte, closes pipe\n- Verifies no timeout occurs and exit code is 0\n- Confirms handler is properly installed\n\n---\n\n### 3. **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** - DiffTest Struct Definition\n\n**DiffTest Fields:**\n- `Name string`: Subtest name (used with `t.Run()`)\n- `Args []string`: Command-line arguments\n- `Stdin []byte`: Input data (nil = EOF, []byte{} = open-then-close)\n- `Env []string`: Environment overrides (merged with inherited env + LC_ALL=C default)\n- `WorkDir string`: Working directory (defaults to temp dir if empty)\n- `ExitCode int`: Expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n- `Normalize []NormalizeFunc`: Output normalization functions applied to stdout/stderr\n- `ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte`: Files to verify were created\n\n**Helper Types & Functions:**\n- `NormalizeFunc`: Type alias for `func([]byte) []byte` for output transformation\n- `TimestampNormalizer`: Built-in normalizer for timestamp patterns\n- `RunDiffTests()`: Runs all tests with identical inputs to both binaries\n- `ComposeNormalizers()`: Combines multiple normalizers\n\n**Test Execution Flow:**\n1. Runs binary with args + stdin in working directory\n2. Applies normalizers to stdout/stderr\n3. Compares stdout, stderr, and exit code with reference binary\n4. Checks expected files exist with correct content\n\n---\n\n### 4. **pkg/testutils/build.go** - BuildBinary Signature\n\n**Function Signature:**\n```go\nfunc BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `t *testing.T`: Test context for fatal error handling\n- `dir string`: Package directory to compile (e.g., \".\")\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Resolves package name from directory\n- Creates temp directory for binary output\n- Executes `go build -o <binPath> <dir>`\n- Returns path to compiled binary\n- Fatals on build failure with combined output\n\n**Usage Pattern:**\n```go\ngoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. **pkg/sys/sigpipe.go** - InstallSIGPIPEHandler Implementation\n\n**Function Signature:**\n```go\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n```\n\n**Implementation Details:**\n- Creates buffered channel: `c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)`\n- Registers for SIGPIPE: `signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)`\n- Spawns goroutine: `go func() { <-c; os.Exit(0) }()`\n- Safe to call multiple times (each call adds a goroutine)\n- Returns immediately; signal handling is async\n\n**Important Notes:**\n- Uses `signal.Notify()` with buffered channel (not `signal.Ignore()`)\n- Matches GNU coreutils behavior by exiting with code 0 on SIGPIPE\n- Each invocation is independent; multiple calls are safe\n\n---\n\n## Key Patterns Summary for New cmd/ Utilities\n\n1. **Header**: Copyright, SPDX license, descriptive package comment with spec reference\n2. **Imports**: Include `syscall`, `errors`, and `pkg/sys`\n3. **SIGPIPE**: Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main()\n4. **Error Handling**: Check for `syscall.EPIPE` and exit(0) appropriately\n5. **Flag Parsing**: Global flag vars with parseFlags function\n6. **Testing**: Use `testutils.DiffTest` with reference binary comparison via `RunDiffTests()`\n7. **SIGPIPE Test**: Include test that verifies handler prevents hanging\n8. **File Output**: Verify expected files with `ExpectedFiles` map in tests\n\nAll files are located in the worktree at:\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5381/`"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0623da15-c329-4680-a15b-3ed66e62b00b","uuid":"63af8c51-f5d3-4fb7-92ab-63eacf4d1c2e","timestamp":"2026-05-20T22:59:42.251Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand patterns us